{title: Bringing in the Sheaves}
{artist: Knowles Shaw / George Minor}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{key_original: C}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Sowing in the morning, sowing seeds of kindness
[D]Sowing in the noontide and the dewy [G]eve
Waiting for the harvest and the [C]time of reaping
We shall [G]come rejoi[D]cing, bringing in the [G]sheaves
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Bringing in the sheaves, bringing in the sheaves
We shall [D]come rejoicing, bringing in the [G]sheaves
Bringing in the sheaves, bringing in the sheaves
We shall [C]come rejoi[G]cing, bringing in the [D]sheaves[G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Sowing in the sunshine, sowing in the shadows
[D]Fearing neither clouds nor winter's chilling [G]breeze
By and by the harvest and the [C]labor ended
We shall [G]come rejoi[D]cing, bringing in the [G]sheaves
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Going forth with weeping, sowing for the Master
[D]Though the loss sustained our spirit often [G]grieves
When our weeping's [C]over, He will bid us welcome
We shall [G]come rejoi[D]cing, bringing in the [G]sheaves
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
